<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="006" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Events capability extraction and must-not-leak proofs</title>
    <phase>0 Removal, prerequisites and seams</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api, auth and tenant-isolation; refactors EventEndpoints statics (.cs) into a capability with frozen REST bytes</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive extraction (caller-scoped reads, per-route record-access filters, Create/AppendTo checks) across a 1,485-line endpoint file with byte-for-byte REST preservation</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs, new Services/Events/** and the events tests; registers in WorkspaceModule.cs (no other Group A task edits it); does not edit Program.cs or EndpointMappingExtensions.cs (task 001)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, refactoring, auth, tenant-isolation, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Extract the get, list, create and complete logic from the Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs statics into an events capability that takes the request context (the IDecisionCapability pattern), keep every REST response byte-for-byte unchanged (frozen-bytes tests first), and add must-not-leak tests proving a caller never sees another user's private event through list or get.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in Minimal API refactoring, Dataverse impersonation and caller-scoped authorization.</role>
  <goal>IEventsCapability / EventsCapability own list, get, create and complete with their authorization; EventEndpoints' four handlers delegate to it; frozen-bytes tests recorded before the change pass after it; must-not-leak tests pass; tasks 025 and 036 can call the capability from MCP tools without copying checks.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-07 part 1 and FR-15. EventEndpoints.cs holds the logic in statics: list GetEventsAsync :437 (route :105), get GetEventByIdAsync :651 (:117), create CreateEventAsync :710 (:129, filter ValidateCreateEventRequestAsync :296), complete CompleteEventAsync :1318 (:170). The header (:29-40) documents the authorization: the list query runs impersonated as the caller; get and complete carry RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter on sprk_events({id}) (no Read → uniform 404; Read without the right → 403); create checks the caller's Create privilege on sprk_event and AppendTo on the regarding record, then writes app-only. IEventDataverseService (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IEventDataverseService.cs) authenticates as the BFF identity. Reviews: unified-access-control-r2 (auth diff), ontology-platform-r1 (capability extraction).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Events/IEventsCapability.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Events/EventsCapability.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/WorkspaceModule.cs (AddScoped&lt;IEventsCapability, EventsCapability&gt;)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Events/EventRoutesContractBaselineTests.cs (frozen bytes, recorded before the refactor)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Events/EventCallerScopeTests.cs (must-not-leak)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/IDecisionCapability.cs and DecisionCapability.cs (capability taking HttpContext/ClaimsPrincipal; registered SignalsModule.cs:138)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/SignalRoutesContractBaselineTests.cs (frozen-bytes model)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Events/EventEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs (existing authorization contract; must pass unchanged)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies/>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Record the frozen-bytes baselines (status code, headers that matter, and body bytes for success, 400, 403 and 404 cases of list, get, create and complete) BEFORE changing EventEndpoints.cs, commit them, and keep them unchanged afterwards (spec MUST: REST bytes unchanged).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">The capability is the single owner of event list/get/create/complete rules; EventEndpoints' four handlers become thin adapters that bind the request, call the capability with the request HttpContext, and map the result. Refile and due-assignee routes stay as they are (out of scope).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The per-route checks (RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter on get/complete, ValidateCreateEventRequestAsync on create, the impersonated list query) are reachable from the capability so an MCP tool gets them without a copy: either the capability enforces them and the REST filter calls the same shared method, or the filter stays and the capability calls the same method; never two implementations. Choose the option that keeps REST Dataverse call counts and bytes unchanged and record the choice.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every capability method takes the request HttpContext (or ClaimsPrincipal) from its caller and fails closed with UserContextRequired when it is null or unauthenticated; nothing falls back to an app-only read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Must-not-leak (FR-15): with two callers A and B and an event private to A, B's list never contains it (all pages, and the count) and B's get returns the uniform 404. If either proof fails, do not ship the extraction on top of a leak: change the read to run as the caller (spec Assumptions) and escalate for uac-r2 review before merging.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Register only in WorkspaceModule.cs (or, if events services are registered elsewhere, that module; record which); do not edit Program.cs, EndpointMappingExtensions.cs, SignalsModule.cs or AuthorizationModule.cs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Logs added carry event id, caller-resolution outcome, row count, timing and reason codes only; no subject, description or regarding names.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master and /conflict-check. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress.</constraint>
  </constraints>

