  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Write EventRoutesContractBaselineTests recording the current bytes for list, get, create and complete (success, 400, 403, 404); run them green against the unchanged code; commit.</step>
    <step order="2">Write EventCallerScopeTests (must-not-leak for list incl. paging and count, and get) against the unchanged code; if they fail, stop and follow the must-not-leak constraint.</step>
    <step order="3">Add IEventsCapability / EventsCapability; move the four handlers' logic into it per the ADR-008 constraint; register it.</step>
    <step order="4">Turn the four handlers into thin adapters; run the baselines, the caller-scope tests, EventEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests and the existing events tests.</step>
    <step order="5">Measure the publish-size delta; run the CVE check; write the proposed CAPABILITY-INDEX row in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/capability-index-pending.md.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a must-not-leak proof fails on the unchanged code, STOP before refactoring: report the leak (it is a live defect), propose the run-as-caller change, and wait for uac-r2 / owner direction.</trigger>
    <trigger>If keeping the REST bytes requires behaviour in the adapter beyond binding and mapping (a check, a retry, a write), STOP and escalate: the capability must be the single owner.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row "Tasks (events)": logic in EventEndpoints statics (:437, :651, :710, :1318) with 8 dependencies; verdict "Extend by extraction" (r1 B-1 style). CAPABILITY-INDEX: no events-capability row (grep "Event" .claude/patterns/CAPABILITY-INDEX.md).</existing>
    <extension>The capability is the extension: the same rules move out of endpoint statics so REST and MCP call one owner; the statics cannot be called by an MCP tool without an HttpRequest binding and endpoint filters.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Tasks 025 and 036 would copy endpoint logic and its authorization into tools, giving task create/complete two owners (ADR-002) and a second place for the caller-scope rule to drift.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test, dotnet publish</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Events/IEventsCapability.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Events/EventsCapability.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Events/EventRoutesContractBaselineTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Events/EventCallerScopeTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">EventRoutesContractBaselineTests, committed before the refactor, pass unchanged after it for list, get, create and complete (success, 400, 403, 404).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">EventEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests and the existing events tests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (must-not-leak): caller B's list (every page and the total count) never contains caller A's private event, and B's get on it returns the uniform 404.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a capability call with a null HttpContext or an unauthenticated principal returns UserContextRequired and makes no Dataverse call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a create without Create privilege on sprk_event, or without AppendTo on the regarding record, is refused through the capability with the same reason as REST and writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep shows each of the four checks implemented once (no duplicated RecordRouteAccess or Create/AppendTo logic between EventEndpoints.cs and EventsCapability.cs).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (total at or under 60 MB), no new HIGH CVE, and the uac-r2 and ontology-r1 reviews.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-07, FR-15; plan risk R2. Two adversarial-verifier passes (auth, tenant-isolation). Seeding proof requested for the must-not-leak list test only: break the caller filter, confirm the test fails, restore.</notes>

